## One next bounded implementation slice

Add a distinct inactive **v2 trusted authority issuer**, using `service/voice-issuance.server.ts` as preserved v1 reference, the unchanged local P3b AES-GCM/HMAC helpers, and the new v2 parent/pre-issuance/issuance ports. The concrete gap is now releasing a newly sealed authority only after its exact parent-bound fingerprint registration and final current-state verification. The existing issuer requires an expiring v1 session fence and cannot consume the new observations; adapting a transport alone does not implement this behavior.

Keep owner/session/parent version derived from mandatory request-bound trusted Auth and the owned service snapshot. Preserve exact lifecycle/revision/source/incarnation, conservative initial verification time, fresh rechecks around waits, shrink-only eligibility and one immutable registration identity. Treat committed lost/malformed/late registration as retained evidence, not rollback or permission to retry with a new identity. Only a new locally sealed envelope can be registered; no old/browser token adoption or v1 fallback. Test the actual SQL chain and local crypto with fictional Auth, including changed Auth/parent/legacy fence/current-thread/service state and late replies. Do not change completed P3b sealing semantics, introduce a generic host wrapper, connect a route or call real Auth/model/voice services. Downstream v2 proof/cleanup/admission/capacity, deployed Auth policy/revocation and quiesced no-fallback cutover remain separate unfinished gates.

